    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Passage 1 　\t词数 407"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "It was a reading class. While all her classmates were flying through the 2nd and 3rd books in the Harry Potter series, Skye Malik, only on page four of the first book, got impossibly stuck on the word “doughnut”."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Her unexpected difficulty with reading is called dyslexia. Skye got a professional diagnosis at the end of the 2nd grade. Knowing that other kids were going through the same thing made it easier on her somehow. What wasn’t easy, even after all the help she got from special tutors and reading programs, was fluent reading. What many people do without thinking—reading—she had to struggle with word by word, sometimes letter by letter. In class, she would hear the other kids flip through the pages on assignments and go on to the questions while she was still battling with the first paragraph."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "section-legacy",
      "title": "旧卷综合题型",
      "instructions": [],
      "layout": "flow",
      "groups": [
        {
          "id": "group-legacy",
          "instructions": [],
          "stimulusBlocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Passage 1 　\t词数 407"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "It was a reading class. While all her classmates were flying through the 2nd and 3rd books in the Harry Potter series, Skye Malik, only on page four of the first book, got impossibly stuck on the word “doughnut”."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Her unexpected difficulty with reading is called dyslexia. Skye got a professional diagnosis at the end of the 2nd grade. Knowing that other kids were going through the same thing made it easier on her somehow. What wasn’t easy, even after all the help she got from special tutors and reading programs, was fluent reading. What many people do without thinking—reading—she had to struggle with word by word, sometimes letter by letter. In class, she would hear the other kids flip through the pages on assignments and go on to the questions while she was still battling with the first paragraph."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "She was as frustrated as she was discouraged. But she didn’t know of any other way until her 4th grade teacher, Miss Pollock, told her about something called Learning Ally."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Learning Ally is a non-profit organization that offers audio-books. A crew of volunteer readers have recorded 75,000 classic novels, children’s books, and school textbooks that help more than 300,000 students and adults with dyslexia or who are blind. Now Skye could listen to the books with her ears and follow the words with her eyes on the page. Instead of having her mother read her textbooks to her, she could independently do her work. “With Learning Ally, I feel confident and capable and can easily keep up with my classmates,” Skye explains, “and I want other kids to feel empowered, just the way I did.”"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "So Skye created The Paco Project which was named after her grandfather, whose nickname was “Paco”. The Paco Project is a fundraiser and educational initiative focusing on giving students with dyslexia access to the same Learning Ally technology that changed her life."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Skye has realized that she is one of the lucky kids who have been diagnosed. She knows that educating teachers about dyslexia and giving students with the learning challenge the tools they need is a great first step in meeting dyslexia head-on, and helping them be confident, capable students."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "“Right now they feel ashamed, unsure and insecure about their school work. If I could help stop these students feeling this way, that would mean the world to me.”"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1.According to the passage, Skye 　　　. "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "A.found out a way with the help of Miss Pollock"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "B.felt annoyed at being teased by her classmates"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "C.preferred reading the first book of Harry Potter "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "D.was diagnosed with dyslexia in her fourth grade"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "2.The Paco Project was created 　　　. "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "A.to promote Learning Ally technology"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "B.to empower those with reading difficulties"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "C.with inspiration from Skye’s grandfather"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "D.in response to the growing demands of teachers"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
